#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:5 9b924a984cb147449c8f83776f555525
msgid "GCS Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:6 56710ed918c4438e828b7e2835b5079e
msgid ""
"Significant improvements have been made in Copter-4.0 and later for "
"Ground Control Failsafe ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:8 724761b28f80442687c3822128b8a61a
msgid ""
"The Ground Station Control (GCS) failsafe controls how Copter will behave"
" if contact with the GCS is lost.  The GCS failsafe monitors the time "
"since the last MAVLink heartbeat from the GCS.  If no heartbeat is "
"received :ref:`FS_GCS_TIMEOUT<FS_GCS_TIMEOUT>` seconds (Default is 5 "
"seconds), the GCS failsafe event will trigger based on your parameter "
"settings. Note that if no GCS is ever connected, the GCS failsafe will "
"remain inactive regardless of parameter settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:12 937960cf1be548578dca23e7474da79b
msgid ""
"Copter also supports other failsafes: :ref:`Radio <radio-failsafe>`, "
":ref:`Battery <failsafe-battery>`, and :ref:`EKF / DCM Check <ekf-inav-"
"failsafe>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:15 410e41637c7f44aebe1ce26ef29a04c4
msgid "When the failsafe will trigger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:17 53f3b911549a40c68b454b5d61d3f978
msgid ""
"The following situations can cause a loss of GCS MAVLink heartbeat, "
"triggering a GCS failsafe event after "
":ref:`FS_GCS_TIMEOUT<FS_GCS_TIMEOUT>` seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:19 f460a220be824138aff54ba2ed1c8134
msgid "The operator turns off or otherwise disconnects the GCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:20 c06896532d3f4987beaf37f69ff5025e
msgid "The copter travels beyond the range of the  GCS telemetry radios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:21 44281ae1a79e4f42bbfe0ccebdb8021f
msgid "The GCS telemetry radio on either end loses power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:22 83b46ee76a454521a3fb3e9030cc3619
msgid ""
"Wires connecting the GCS telemetry radio to the autopilot or ground "
"equipment become disconnected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:25 50283e9c9e7f4bac93d89dd3281a086b
msgid "What will happen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:27 2a579602f2f34191b16f19ef73871e0e
msgid ""
"When a GCS failsafe is triggered, the copter can be configured via "
"parameters to do nothing, land immediately, RTL, or SmartRTL.  It can "
"also be configured to bypass the failsafe in an Auto Mode mission, bypass"
" the failsafe in pilot controlled modes, or to continue landing if "
"already in a landing phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:29 64f9aff9690b45b9b33eded4b6dcee03
msgid "If the copter is disarmed, no failsafe will take place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:30 2d372cd74f3345f4a46b742ed5a53d64
msgid "If the copter is armed but has landed, the copter will immediately disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:31 a9fb1bc1a89b4c05845baf403ac27388
msgid ""
"If the copter is armed in Stabilize or Acro modes, and the throttle input"
" is at minimum, the copter will immediately disarm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:32 8462304d69534e81a0589f89e70d61da
msgid ""
"Otherwise, the copter will take the actions as configured in the "
"parameters described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:34 3c4fa043b5cc42ed982241cd2c5829b4
msgid ""
"If the failsafe clears (i.e. GCS reconnects and MAVLink heartbeat is "
"restored) the copter will remain in its failsafe mode. It will **not** "
"automatically return to the flight mode that was active before the "
"failsafe was triggered. This means that if, for example, the vehicle was "
"in Loiter when the failsafe occurred and the flight mode was "
"automatically changed to RTL, even after the GCS reconnects, the vehicle "
"would remain in RTL.  If the pilot wished to re-take control in Loiter "
"he/she would need to change the flight mode switch to another position "
"and then back to Loiter. This can be done via the re-connected GCS also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:37 da700a0a382f46a98f3d6b26d508bec9
msgid "Setting the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:39 064bb60163a64a57b2bea9a77f3a8a2d
msgid ""
"In Mission Planner's  full parameter list or full parameter tree, set the"
" :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABLE <FS_GCS_ENABLE>` parameter to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:41 b0365366521b47aabbface5ba8d0a7f6
msgid "**Disabled** (Value 0) will disable the GCS failsafe entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:42 1797ca1d154e4b9195707fae4438ff19
msgid ""
"**Enabled Always RTL** (Value 1) will switch the copter to RTL Mode.  If "
"the GPS position is not usable, the copter will change to Land Mode "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:43 54c6c74fbdbf4e1fa236025dace468f2
msgid ""
"**Enabled Continue with Mission in Auto Mode (this value has no effect in"
" 4.0 and later with FS_OPTION parameter replacing function, see below )**"
" (Value 2) will ignore the failsafe in an Auto Mode mission. Otherwise, "
"it will behave the same as *Enabled Always RTL*. This option no longer "
"exists in Copter 4.0 and later. Instead, see the "
":ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter for this function. Setting this "
"value in Copter 4.0 and later version will automatically be converted and"
" set to Value 1 (Always RTL) and the :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` "
"bitmask will be modified to include bit (1) for \"Continue auto mode "
"mission on GCS failsafe\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:44 35831123c6814d738442fab8c5477674
msgid ""
"**Enabled SmartRTL or RTL** (Value 3) will switch the copter to SmartRTL "
"mode. If SmartRTL is not available, the copter will switch to RTL Mode "
"instead.  If the GPS position is not usable, the copter will change to "
"Land Mode instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:45 35773db2954e474497873c16413dbb13
msgid ""
"**Enabled SmartRTL or Land** (Value 4) will switch the copter to SmartRTL"
" mode. If SmartRTL is not available, the copter will switch to Land Mode "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:46 f83ff63dccf442c9a967e2393dd66f49
msgid "**Enabled Always Land** (Value 5) will switch the copter to Land Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:47 94348046872448399c8fde0d1d5545cf
msgid ""
"**Auto DO_LAND_START or RTL** (Value 6) will execute a DO_LAND_START auto"
" mission sequence or and RTL if no DO_LAND_START sequence exists(see :ref"
":`common-do-land-start`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:48 2f357a84681d442a99845c37841d25d3
msgid ""
"**BRAKE or LAND** (Value 7): switch to BRAKE mode if included in firmware"
" or to LAND mode, if not included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:49 e71d68739ed84124ac21159aec139f34
msgid ""
"Any invalid value (Such as accidentally enter 99 as a parameter value) "
"will will behave the same as **Enabled Always RTL**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:51 88b1120ecd9c4a0baad06557eb15bc7f
msgid ""
"The :ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` parameter (Copter 4.0 and later) is a "
"bitmask parameter to select one or more options that modify the standard "
"actions of the radio, GCS, and battery failsafe. In the Mission Planner "
"full parameter list or full parameter tree, the handy checkbox popup "
"window is an easy what to set this (and any other bitmask) parameter. Be "
"sure to go to Help > Check Beta Updates to pull the latest parameter "
"definitions first while connected to the internet. The "
":ref:`FS_OPTIONS<FS_OPTIONS>` bits are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:53 0b3b0aeb32454165a9ac49e8537390e2
msgid ""
"bit 0 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-"
"failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:54 28b27275e92d4415a0bbc31bf1ddf141
msgid ""
"bit 1 set: Continue if in auto mode on :ref:`Ground Control Station "
"Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:55 405f905b7c1d4703bbe5c96ddaa520a2
msgid ""
"bit 2 set: Continue if in guided mode :ref:`Radio Failsafe <radio-"
"failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:56 66cc3d1dcc064275a337657a3a95c276
msgid "bit 3 set: Continue if landing on any failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:57 23e4e6874fb843f8acaf8ebfecf93c2f
msgid ""
"bit 4 set: Continue in pilot control on :ref:`Ground Control Station "
"Failsafe<gcs-failsafe>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:58 5feb8bb70ac4444a9a834f78fbb862ef
msgid ""
"If none of the above are set, then execute the :ref:`FS_GCS_ENABLE "
"<FS_GCS_ENABLE>` option as configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:60 d0373a8766494dfbb979a9c31eaa90de
msgid ""
"Only bitmask bits 1, 3, & 4 affect actions taken during GCS failsafe. "
"This parameter also works in conjunction with the battery and radio "
"failsafe, so ensure you are taking all options into account when setting "
"this parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/gcs-failsafe.rst:67 16b80c9d5fff4e998aba93ebdfa5e5ba
msgid ""
"All Failsafe Parameters can be observed or set from the Advanced "
"Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

